# What EAS Build uploads for the phone app. EAS reads this file at the git
# root (not app/), and it replaces .gitignore for the upload, so it must repeat
# the important exclusions. Only app/ is needed; the native folders are
# generated on the build server from app.json (CNG), and a local one would be
# used verbatim.
#
# Gitignore syntax: a pattern without a leading slash matches at any depth, so
# the repo-root folders are anchored with "/" (an unanchored "src/" would also
# drop app/src, which broke a build).
/.pio/
/.vscode/
/.claude/
/docs/
/firmware/
/hardware/
/legacy/
/tools/
*.csv
*.mp4
*.log
/app/node_modules/
/app/android/
/app/ios/
/app/.expo/
/app/dist/
/app/web-build/
/app/coverage/
/app/store/
/app/credentials.json
*.jks
.DS_Store
